[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Last One?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.39]For how long did the writer give up smoking? | 作者戒烟戒了多长时间？
[00:15.78]After reading an article entitled 'Cigarette Smoking and Your Health' I lit a cigarette to calm my nerves. | 读完一篇题为《吸烟与健康》的文章后，我点燃了一支香烟，以便使神经平静下来。
[00:26.25]I smoked with concentration and pleasure as I was sure that this would be my last cigarette. | 我聚精会神而又愉快地吸着这支烟，因为我确信这将是我最后一支烟。
[00:35.11]For a whole week I did not smoke at all and during this time my wife suffered terribly. | 整整一个星期我根本没有吸烟，在此期间我妻子吃尽了苦头。
[00:43.84]I had all the usual symptoms of someone giving up smoking: a bad temper and an enormous appetite. | 我具备了戒烟者通常有的一切症状：脾气暴躁和食欲旺盛。
[00:53.83]My friends kept on offering me cigarettes and cigars. | 我的朋友们不断地向我递香烟和雪茄。
[00:59.15]They made no effort to hide their amusement whenever I produced a packet of sweets from my pocket. | 每当我从口袋里掏出一袋糖果时，他们都毫不掩饰地表现出非常好笑的样子。
[01:08.29]After seven days of this I went to a party. | 这样过了7天后，我去参加了一个聚会。
[01:13.04]Everybody around me was smoking and I felt extremely uncomfortable. | 我周围的人都吸烟，我感到非常不自在。
[01:19.78]When my old friend Brian urged me to accept a cigarette, it was more than I could bear. | 当我的老朋友布赖恩极力劝我接受一支香烟时，我实在忍不住了。
[01:29.23]I took one guiltily, lit it and smoked with satisfaction. | 我内疚地接过一支点上，心满意足地抽了起来。
[01:35.71]My wife was delighted that things had returned to normal once more. | 一切又恢复了正常，为此我妻子非常高兴。
[01:41.63]Anyway, as Brian pointed out, it is the easiest thing in the world to give up smoking. | 不管怎么说，正如布赖恩指出的那样，戒烟是世界上最容易的事。
[01:50.01]He himself has done it lots of times! | 他自己就已戒了很多次了！
